expr('d_ailleurs','d’ailleurs',[183],'besides; moreover',[],'',[],'','The philosopher adds that the remote rulers, rather than the soldiers alone, deserve punishment. The VI full-span bank and its published component identity were inspected and reused unchanged. This is an additional argument, not spatial elsewhere; final import must retain the published meaning with no duplicate component mastery.',earlier=('chapter-06-expression-review-01.json','d_ailleurs'))
expr('nulle_part','nulle part',[170],'nowhere; in no place',['elsewhere','everywhere','somewhere'],'Il affirme ne trouver le bonheur dans aucun lieu : il ne l’a vu ___.',['nulle part','ailleurs','partout','quelque part'],'Quelle locution négative signifie dans aucun lieu ?','Nulle part denies any location where the traveler has found true happiness. The four full phrases fit the negated seeing construction; lack of a place differs from another place, every place or an unspecified place. Part is neither a portion noun nor the verb departing in this span.')
expr('de_bonne_foi','de bonne foi',[171],'honestly; sincerely',['reluctantly','in secret','dishonestly'],'Il avoue sincèrement ce qu’il croit vrai, sans tromper son interlocuteur : il le dit ___.',['de bonne foi','à contrecœur','en secret','de mauvaise foi'],'Quelle locution indique une déclaration sincère faite sans intention de tromper ?','The frank philosopher candidly admits widespread folly and unhappiness. The earlier VII expression draft has no approved questions; its sincerity disposition was checked, then these three bands were authored. All adverbial choices fit le dit, while honesty rather than reluctance, secrecy or insincerity selects the phrase. Bonne is not a maid and foi is not a promised word.')
expr('s_agit','s’agit',[175,177,178],'is about; concerns',['happens','proceeds','is spent'],'La querelle a pour objet ce tas de boue : il ___ de ce tas.',['s’agit','provient','reste','manque'],'Quelle construction impersonnelle signifie est question de quelque chose ?','The three impersonal clauses name what the quarrel concerns, including negation of the claimed motive. The global agir family already has sns_zola_s_agir_concern, distinct from accomplishing an action. Prepare this full fused pronominal surface on that existing meaning, not a second expression sense. The middle alternatives are syntactically possible with de ce tas, while the stated subject of the dispute selects s’agit. Final import must bridge the whole span and suppress s’/agit duplicate encounters.','retain_published_meaning_full_span_import_reconciliation:sns_zola_s_agir_concern')
expr('en_use','en use',[173],'behaves; acts in that manner',['wears it down','uses a tool','makes a purchase'],'Pour dire qu’on agit ainsi envers autrui, le récit emploie « on ___ ainsi ».',['en use','le détériore','se sert d’un outil','fait un achat'],'Quelle construction signifie agit de cette manière, notamment envers autrui ?','Académie 7 user explicitly records absolute en user for acting in a particular manner. The global proper user verb has only wear-down, so prepare this distinct behaving meaning under lem_fr_user_verb. This is how humans wage war, not deterioration by rubbing. All middle predicates are grammatical; behavior rather than wearing an object, using a tool or purchasing selects the whole construction. No anaphoric en encounter is duplicated.','new_sense_existing_lemma:lem_fr_user_verb')
expr('de_temps_immemorial','de temps immémorial',[173],'since time beyond living memory',['since yesterday','for a moment','for the first time'],'Ce comportement dure depuis une époque si ancienne qu’aucun souvenir n’en marque le début : on agit ainsi ___.',['de temps immémorial','depuis hier','pour un instant','pour la première fois'],'Quelle locution renvoie à une ancienneté dont on ne garde pas le souvenir du commencement ?','The philosopher presents warfare as having persisted beyond remembered beginnings. The bank tests the phrase’s temporal meaning, not a factual date of the first war. All four temporal phrases fit the verb; remote unremembered antiquity selects the target. The noun temps and adjective immémorial remain inside the full-span identity.')
expr('d_accord','d’accord',[185],'in agreement; agreed',['in conflict','in doubt','in a hurry'],'Ils partagent la même opinion sur ces points : ils sont ___.',['d’accord','en désaccord','dans le doute','dans l’urgence'],'Quelle locution signifie que plusieurs personnes partagent une même opinion ?','The philosophers agree on two or three understood points, contrasting their many disputes. The full agreeing predicate is prepared, excluding generic de and musical accord. Each alternative fits ils sont; shared opinion rather than disagreement, uncertainty or urgency selects agreement. Published d’accord component meanings require one canonical full-span route before import.')
expr('du_tout','du tout',[198,204],'at all; whatsoever',['sometimes','probably','already'],'Il n’en comprend absolument rien : il ne le comprend pas ___.',['du tout','encore','entièrement','vraiment'],'Quelle locution renforce une négation en excluant toute quantité ou tout degré ?','Point du tout and rien du tout reinforce a complete negation, concerning understanding and action respectively. They are not the quantity pronoun tout standing for everything. All adverbs fit the negative completion while absolute exclusion alone selects du tout; each complete source span is retained to suppress duplicate component mastery.')
expr('tout_haut','tout haut',[195],'aloud; audibly',['silently','in secret','inwardly'],'Il prononce les paroles de manière audible, plutôt que dans sa tête : il les dit ___.',['tout haut','en silence','en secret','intérieurement'],'Quelle locution signifie de manière audible, par opposition à intérieurement ?','The Peripatetic says the proposition aloud. Haut is not spatial elevation, and tout intensifies the established vocal expression. All four manner phrases fit les dit; audibility rather than silence, secrecy or an inward thought selects tout haut. Before import reconcile any existing haut loud meaning into one whole-span route rather than duplicate word and phrase encounters.')
expr('en_dedans','en dedans',[191],'inside; within',['outside','above','nearby'],'Ils prétendent connaître leur être intérieur : ce qui est à l’intérieur se trouve ___.',['en dedans','en dehors','au-dessus','tout près'],'Quelle locution désigne l’intérieur, en opposition à l’extérieur ?','The giant contrasts what is outside the philosophers with their interior soul and thinking. This figurative inward domain retains the inside/outside opposition; it does not mean bodily location alone. All four locative phrases fit se trouve. The whole locution is prepared so en is not incorrectly treated as a partitive pronoun.')
expr('de_nouveau','de nouveau',[199],'again; once more',['for the first time','forever','in advance'],'Elle doit apprendre encore une fois ce qu’elle aurait déjà su : elle l’apprend ___.',['de nouveau','pour la première fois','à jamais','à l’avance'],'Quelle locution indique qu’une action se produit une nouvelle fois ?','The Cartesian claim says the soul must learn everything again; tout remains the pronoun everything outside de nouveau. No adjective meaning new modifies an object here. All temporal phrases fit apprend; repetition rather than first occurrence, indefinite duration or anticipation selects the target.')
expr('de_haut_en_bas','de haut en bas',[210],'with contempt; looking down on someone',['with respect','with curiosity','with indifference'],'Se croyant supérieur, il leur témoigne du mépris : il les regarde ___.',['de haut en bas','avec respect','avec curiosité','avec indifférence'],'Quelle locution, dans regarder quelqu’un, exprime ici un regard méprisant ?','Académie 1762 regarder explicitly gives regarder quelqu’un de haut en bas for showing contempt or disdain. The source’s tiny cleric claims universal knowledge and human primacy before giants; this contextual application is an editorial inference supported by the conventional idiom, rather than a mere vertical survey. The earlier unresolved gaze draft was inspected. All four adverbial phrases fit regarde; contempt rather than respect, curiosity or indifference selects the whole locution.')
expr('je_vous_en_prie','je vous en prie',[185],'please; I ask you politely',['I forbid you','I blame you','I congratulate you'],'Il sollicite poliment une réponse : « Dites-moi, ___, à quoi vous vous occupez. »',['je vous en prie','je vous l’interdis','je vous le reproche','je vous en félicite'],'Quelle formule exprime ici une demande polie ?','The Sirian politely requests an account of the sages’ activities. This source formula is an entreaty, not the response to thanks that identical words can express elsewhere. Each first-person clause fits the quotation; polite requesting rather than prohibition, reproach or congratulation selects it. Je/vous/en/prie components stay within this specific formula.')
expr('en_nombre_rond','en nombre rond',[188],'in round numbers; approximately',['exactly','without a number','in strict order'],'La quantité est donnée sous une forme arrondie, non comme une mesure exacte : elle est exprimée ___.',['en nombre rond','avec exactitude','sans aucun nombre','dans un ordre strict'],'Quelle locution indique une quantité exprimée par un nombre arrondi ?','The philosophers give the lunar distance as a rounded quantity. The question tests rounding and does not endorse a modern astronomical measurement. Each manner phrase fits exprimée; round approximation rather than exactness, absence of a number or ordering selects the target. Nominal rond is not physical circularity here.')
expr('eh_bien','Eh bien',[201],'well then; a prompt to continue the reasoning',['goodbye','thank you','alas'],'Il poursuit son raisonnement à partir de la réponse : « ___, peux-tu expliquer ce que cette chose est ? »',['Eh bien','Au revoir','Merci beaucoup','Hélas'],'Quelle formule introduit ici la prochaine étape d’un raisonnement ?','Micromégas takes up the reported attributes and asks for the underlying nature of matter. The formula advances the exchange, not a claim of good quality, proficiency or willingness. All complete interjections fit the quotation. Published bien discourse meanings must be reconciled into a full formula before import so one occurrence does not generate two encounters.')
expr('ou_bien','ou bien',[205],'or else; introducing another alternative',['and then','therefore','nevertheless'],'Il propose une autre possibilité : « L’âme serait ceci, ___ elle serait cela. »',['ou bien','et puis','par conséquent','pourtant'],'Quelle locution relie ici deux possibilités présentées comme des alternatives ?','Both occurrences introduce an alternative metaphor for soul and body. Every occurrence of ou bien in this unit is indexed, including the second one. Bien does not express knowledge quality or certainty here. All connectors fit the two clauses, while alternatives rather than succession, consequence or opposition select ou bien.')
expr('a_l_heure_que','à l’heure que',[173],'at the time when; as',['before the time when','after the time when','because'],'Pour situer les faits au moment même où il parle, il dit : « Cela arrive ___ je vous parle. »',['à l’heure que','avant que','après que','parce que'],'Quelle construction du récit situe les faits au moment où l’on parle ?','The historical à l’heure que clause states that the warfare is occurring as the philosopher speaks. The temporal relative construction is prepared in full rather than assigning que an unrelated object-relative bank. The first-person parle form works with all four connective alternatives; contemporaneity rather than before, after or cause selects the phrase.')
expr('sans_que','sans que',[204],'without; without it being the case that',['although','because','so that'],'Il affirme que Dieu fait tout sans son intervention : « Il fait tout ___ je m’en mêle. »',['sans que','bien que','parce que','afin que'],'Quelle locution conjonctive exprime l’absence d’une intervention ?','The Malebranchist claims that God acts without his involvement. This is absence of the subordinate action, not the bare sans question under shared repair. The first-person mêle form fits all four conjunctions, with absence versus concession, cause and purpose selecting sans que. The philosophical claim stays attributed to the speaker.')
expr('a_l_occasion_de','à l’occasion de',[206],'in connection with; prompted by',['in spite of','before','instead of'],'Il rapporte sa pensée à ses expériences sensibles : elle apparaît ___ ces expériences.',['à l’occasion de','en dépit de','avant','à la place de'],'Quelle locution relie ici la pensée aux expériences qui lui donnent occasion de se produire ?','The Lockean reports thinking only in connection with his sensory experiences. Occasion names a circumstance giving rise to thinking, not a festive celebration. All prepositional phrases fit ces expériences, while the asserted occasion rather than obstacle, temporal precedence or replacement selects the target. No historical proof of a theory is claimed.')
expr('les_infiniment_petits','les infiniment petits',[213],'the infinitely small beings; the tiny people',['the very large beings','the tall travelers','the adult rulers'],'Le géant donne ce nom aux minuscules êtres humains : il les appelle ___.',['les infiniment petits','les infiniment grands','les grands voyageurs','les souverains adultes'],'Quelle locution nominale désigne ici les êtres humains vus comme extrêmement minuscules ?','The giant names tiny people who nevertheless possess vast pride. This substantivized masculine plural phrase differs from the singular abstract domain l’infiniment petit reviewed in VI. All four complete noun phrases are masculine plural and fit appelle. The full span prevents an isolated article plus an unrelated adjective from becoming duplicated vocabulary identities.')
